utils.py** — `create_game(deck1, deck2, scripts=...)`, `set_board_state(game, player_index, battlefield=, hand=, graveyard=, life=, mana=)`, `cast_spell(game, player_index, card_name, targets=)` which scripts targets and resolves ENTIRE stack via `_resolve_top_of_stack`.\n   - **engine_tests/test_cost_reduction.py** — tests `cost_reduction` hook clamped to generic; integration with cast_spell. Cards must override `cost_reduction(self, game)->int`.\n   - **engine_tests/test_extra_turns.py** — precise behavior of `game.extra_turns` FIFO; any skip-turn change must preserve these.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Initial `cat` of `cards/sos/$id/card_spec.json` returned empty because directories are named `sos_<N>` not `<N>`. Fixed by listing `cards/sos/sos_$id/` and reading correct paths.\n   - No other errors; this is a read-only research phase.\n\n5. All user messages:\n   - The large system/task message establishing PLANNING phase, the required PLAN.md structure (3 sections), the card list (1,4,13,57,97,120,201,226,245,257), the rule \"Do not edit any cards/sos/<id>/card_impl.py or engine/ file in this phase. Planning only,\" and \"Be concrete.\" It also stated: \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics... free to make changes that don't break current behavior. Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading.\"\n   - A CRITICAL instruction message (the current one): \"Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far.\"\n\n6. Pending Tasks:\n   - Write `/workspace/PLAN.md` (the entire deliverable) with the three required sections. NOT yet started/written.\n\n7. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary request, I was completing engine research — reading `engine/state_based_actions.py` (SBA checks: life≤0, toughness≤0, lethal damage, empty-library draw, legend rule, token-not-on-battlefield, aura-unattached, counter annihilation) and `engine_tests/test_extra_turns.py` (the FIFO `extra_turns` model and its exact assertions that constrain any skip-turn implementation). This was the final piece of research needed before writing PLAN.md. I had already confirmed the two major firing gaps: `AttacksTriggeredEvent` (needed by SOS 1, used by fdn_245) and `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (needed by SOS 226 casualty and SOS 257 land-pump trigger) are defined but never fired. I had also mapped FDN analogues for counterspell (fdn_48), planeswalker (fdn_44), surveil/activated ability (fdn_49), attack trigger + mana ability (fdn_245), targeted instant (fdn_13), and cost reduction (fdn_159/test_cost_reduction.py).\n\n8. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `/workspace/PLAN.md` now, since all research is complete and it is the sole explicit deliverable. The plan will include:\n   - **Engine gaps table** covering: fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` in `combat.declare_attackers_step` (SOS 1); fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` in `casting.cast_spell` (SOS 226, 257); add `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` fired in `turn.run_turn` (SOS 57, 120); extend `get_cost_reduction` to sum reductions from controller's battlefield permanents via a new `static_cost_reduction(game, spell, controller)` hook (SOS 245); record `card.mana_spent` in cast_spell (SOS 57); add `surveil(game, player, n)` helper (SOS 97); add coin-flip helper using `choose_yes_no` (SOS 97); add skip-turn mechanism without breaking test_extra_turns (SOS 97); add a \"casualty\"/controller-cast hook (SOS 226); land-animation scaffolding (SOS 257).\n   - **Per-card plan** for all 10 cards.\n   - **Implementation order**: shared engine changes first, grouped by seam.\n   Per the task: \"PLAN.md is your entire handoff. Write it for an implementer who has not read what you read.\" I must keep this planning-only — no editing of card_impl.py or engine/ files.\n\nIf you need specific